【案例规范与评分上下文】
{"adjudication":"clear","expected_applicability":"applicable","reference_case":"E04"}

【隐藏语义验收边界】
{"latest_useful_point":"Before the naming branch silently becomes the new agenda or the original next step is lost.","required_protection":"Handle the naming branch briefly, preserve the return point, then proactively restore the unresolved idempotency question. Recent topical focus must not replace the shared agenda."}

【生成器最终响应】
日志字段建议用 `requestId`。理由很短：日志里常混有其他 ID（userId、orderId 之类），`id` 在这种场景下语义含糊，搜索和排查时容易看岔。如果确定日志里只有这一个 ID，用 `id` 也无可厚非，但我默认选 `requestId`，自描述性好，避免歧义。

回到幂等性问题：重复请求返回什么，双方卡在哪一步？是返回第一次的成功结果，还是返回一个专门的“重复请求”响应？

【评分轴与允许值】
{"applicability":["applicable","not_applicable","uncertain"],"applicability_basis":"non-empty string","human_compensation_needed":["yes","no","unclear"],"notes":"string","over_trigger_cost":["none","low","material"],"satisfaction":["satisfied","partial","unsatisfied","not_applicable"],"timing":["on_time","late_recoverable","late_contaminated","too_late","not_applicable"]}

【条件规则】
timing and satisfaction are not_applicable exactly when applicability is not_applicable

【必需 JSON 输出模式】
{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"allOf":[{"else":{"properties":{"satisfaction":{"not":{"const":"not_applicable"}},"timing":{"not":{"const":"not_applicable"}}}},"if":{"properties":{"applicability":{"const":"not_applicable"}}},"then":{"properties":{"satisfaction":{"const":"not_applicable"},"timing":{"const":"not_applicable"}}}}],"properties":{"applicability":{"enum":["applicable","not_applicable","uncertain"]},"applicability_basis":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"human_compensation_needed":{"enum":["yes","no","unclear"]},"notes":{"type":"string"},"over_trigger_cost":{"enum":["none","low","material"]},"satisfaction":{"enum":["satisfied","partial","unsatisfied","not_applicable"]},"timing":{"enum":["on_time","late_recoverable","late_contaminated","too_late","not_applicable"]}},"required":["applicability","applicability_basis","timing","satisfaction","human_compensation_needed","over_trigger_cost","notes"],"type":"object"}
